---
/*
  Sprint 2H Letters — static reproduction of the immutable golden master's
  Letters view (reference/newsstand-original/source/Newsstand - Full
  Site.dc.html, the `isLetters` sc-if block, ~lines 579-611).

  Content classification (Sprint 2 content-shell rule — see
  DESIGN_DEVIATIONS.md and AGENTS.md):
  - CLASS 1, structural/interface copy: the "Letters / p.34" kicker
    pattern, the "Currently taking" / "Also accepting" card taxonomy.
  - CLASS 2, demo/fictional content pending final Sprint 2 review: the red
    panel's pull-statement and intro copy, the "Currently taking" list, the
    "Also accepting" card body, and both handwritten notes. Reproduced
    verbatim from the golden master's own final copy, character-for-
    character, same as every prior sprint's page-local content.
  - CLASS 3, real-content substitution (project owner's explicit Sprint 2H
    decision, NOT a placeholder pending review): the three contact
    mechanisms. Unlike every other page's copy, this page's whole point is
    to be a genuinely working contact surface, so the email address, the
    GitHub link, and the LinkedIn link are the real, final values —
    jvcaballero@tuta.io, https://github.com/JVCaballero, and
    https://linkedin.com/in/john-vincent-c-06814b111 — displayed in the
    source's own literal-uppercase display convention (e.g.
    "JVCABALLERO@TUTA.IO"). See DESIGN_DEVIATIONS.md for the full writeup.

  Content storage: page-local, matching every prior sprint's precedent —
  there is no `letters` Content Collection scaffold in
  src/content.config.ts, and this sprint does not introduce one.

  GitHub/LinkedIn upgrade: the source's GITHUB.COM/JVCABALLERO and
  LINKEDIN.COM/IN/JVCABALLERO spans carry the exact same visual treatment
  as the email span, but no `onClick` at all — inert, decorative text.
  Production upgrades both to real, functional, external `<a>` links
  (`target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"`), per the project owner's
  explicit Sprint 2H decision — a faithful-looking-but-nonfunctional
  contact row would be a worse production outcome than a real link with
  the identical visual treatment.

  Email mechanism ("replace the prototype plumbing, preserve the
  experience"): the source's email span is a bare `<span onClick={{
  copyEmail }}>` — no href, not a real link, and not keyboard-operable at
  all (a `<span>` with a template onClick is not natively focusable).
  Production replaces it with a real `<a href="mailto:jvcaballero@tuta.io"
  data-copy-email>` — keyboard-focusable, works with no JS via the mailto
  fallback — whose click handler is progressively enhanced by
  src/scripts/interactions/clipboard-copy.ts: if `navigator.clipboard` is
  available, the click is intercepted, the real address is copied, and the
  "copied!" confirmation (already present, verbatim, in the golden master)
  is shown and announced via aria-live. If the Clipboard API is
  unavailable, or the copy attempt itself fails, the mailto navigation
  proceeds untouched and no confirmation is shown. Do NOT use
  `<span onClick>` — every contact method here is a real, native,
  keyboard-operable anchor.

  Heading hierarchy: one <h1> ("Write to the editor"). The two right-column
  cards each get an <h2> ("Currently taking" / "Also accepting"), matching
  the established B-Sides/Rotation card-heading precedent — no other
  heading exists on this page. The red panel's large statement line reads
  as conversational pull-quote-style copy, not a section heading (it has no
  heading role in the source, and nothing on the page is "under" it in a
  document-outline sense), so it is a plain <p>.

  Contact list: a <ul>/<li> of the three contact methods (not a <div>
  stack, as the source uses) — each item is semantically equivalent (one
  contact method), so list semantics are the more accurate reproduction
  than three sibling paragraphs.

  "Currently taking" list: the ▸/✗ glyphs are literal source characters,
  reproduced verbatim as inline text (not a real <li> marker) exactly as
  the source's own div-per-line markup implies — there is no separate,
  redundant list-marker glyph to conflict with real <li> markers, since
  this is a plain <ul> with `list-style:none` and the glyph is the line's
  own leading character, read by a screen reader as ordinary text (which is
  accurate: it is not decorative, it is the actual "included/excluded"
  signal for that line).

  scroll-reveal.ts is extended in this sprint to also match the
  '/letters/' prefix (see src/scripts/interactions/scroll-reveal.ts). The
  two right-column cards carry `data-reveal`, matching the golden master's
  own `data-reveal="1"` on each card div. The red panel and its contents do
  NOT carry `data-reveal`, matching the source exactly.

  New interaction module: src/scripts/interactions/clipboard-copy.ts,
  registered in interaction-controller.ts's MODULES array (the one
  expected exception to leaving that file alone — its own header comment
  describes exactly this kind of extension).

  Focus-visible note: the global `:focus-visible` outline
  (src/styles/global.css) is red-on-whatever, which is invisible against
  this page's own red panel background (`--color-red` outline on a
  `--color-red` fill is the same color). `.letters-contact__link` gets a
  narrowly-scoped `:focus-visible` override to an ink outline instead, so
  all three contact links show a visible focus ring against the red panel
  — a real, new accessibility necessity for this route only, not a design
  deviation (the source has no keyboard-focus concept at all). See
  src/styles/letters.css and DESIGN_DEVIATIONS.md.
*/
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import '../../styles/letters.css';

const title = 'Write to the editor | CABALLERO!';
const description =
  'Letters / p.34 — write to the editor. Real contact methods: email, GitHub, and LinkedIn. Service-offering copy pending final Sprint 2 review.';

const EMAIL = 'jvcaballero@tuta.io';
const EMAIL_DISPLAY = 'JVCABALLERO@TUTA.IO';
const GITHUB_URL = 'https://github.com/JVCaballero';
const GITHUB_DISPLAY = 'GITHUB.COM/JVCABALLERO';
const LINKEDIN_URL = 'https://linkedin.com/in/john-vincent-c-06814b111';
const LINKEDIN_DISPLAY = 'LINKEDIN.COM/IN/JVCABALLERO';
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <div class="letters-page container">
    <p class="letters-kicker">Letters / p.34</p>
    <h1 class="letters-headline">Write to the editor</h1>

    <div class="letters-grid">
      <div class="letters-panel">
        <p class="letters-panel__statement">
          Got a weird problem in an unglamorous industry? That's the good stuff.
        </p>
        <p class="letters-panel__intro">
          Contract or full-time, web or mobile, greenfield or a decade-old mess
          someone is embarrassed about. I read everything and reply within two
          days &mdash; faster if you lead with the actual problem instead of the
          tech stack.
        </p>

        <ul class="letters-contact">
          <li>
            <a
              class="letters-contact__link"
              href={`mailto:${EMAIL}`}
              data-copy-email={EMAIL}
            >
              {EMAIL_DISPLAY}
            </a>
          </li>
          <li>
            <a
              class="letters-contact__link"
              href={GITHUB_URL}
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
            >
              {GITHUB_DISPLAY}
            </a>
          </li>
          <li>
            <a
              class="letters-contact__link"
              href={LINKEDIN_URL}
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
            >
              {LINKEDIN_DISPLAY}
            </a>
          </li>
        </ul>

        <p
          class="letters-copied"
          data-copy-confirmation
          role="status"
          aria-live="polite"
          hidden
        >
          copied! now tell me the actual problem &rarr;
        </p>
        <p class="letters-hand-note">
          tap the address &mdash; it copies itself
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="letters-sidebar">
        <div class="letters-card" data-reveal>
          <h2 class="letters-card__heading">Currently taking</h2>
          <ul class="letters-taking">
            <li>&#9656; Contract builds from <strong>November 2026</strong></li>
            <li>&#9656; AI workflow audits (2&ndash;3 weeks)</li>
            <li>&#9656; Rescue jobs on stalled products</li>
            <li class="letters-taking__excluded">
              &#10007; Unpaid &ldquo;quick logo tweaks&rdquo;, respectfully
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="letters-card letters-card--highlight" data-reveal>
          <h2 class="letters-card__heading">Also accepting</h2>
          <p>
            Gig bookings, band arrangement requests, and strong opinions about
            which gacha banner I should have skipped.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
